2026-10-26T22:38:13Z  CHANGE    Slice 2: the library-and-playlist mutation cluster left SunoBridge for its own class, `src/qml_bridge/SunoMutationsSection.hpp/.cpp` (QObject child of the bridge). It owns the `vc::suno::SunoLibraryMutations` lifetime, the eleven captured verbs, the clip-scoped vs playlist-scoped routing, the `update_type` string map and the refusal for an unmapped member. The service is still the single owner of every request body, so no second owner of the wire format exists.
2026-10-26T22:38:13Z  CHANGE    The QML surface is unchanged: same singleton, same property and invokable names, same signal names, same argument order. The bridge keeps the forwarders and relays the section's signals; `clipMutationSettled`/`playlistMutationSettled` still carry (id, verb, outcome, reason), and a refusal still reaches `errorMessage` exactly once.
2026-10-26T22:38:13Z  CHANGE    Lifetime rules preserved: the service is created with the section as its parent, dropped on sign-out (`signOutSuno` and controller detach) so no resolver pointer into a replaced `SunoAccountManager` survives, and re-pointed — not rebuilt — when the controller is swapped, because the resolver lives inside the account manager. The gate-verdict move still re-publishes `mutationsAvailable` without a spurious `mutationsBusy`.
2026-10-26T22:38:13Z  CHANGE    New test suite `tests/unit/qml_bridge/test_SunoMutationsSection.cpp` pins the seam the extraction created: unattached = unavailable with a sentence; an unmapped `update_type` settles `refused` on the playlist channel only, with a reason naming the four captured members and one visible failure; the four captured members settle nothing without a service; every verb is a safe no-op without a service; detach with no service announces nothing.
