2026-10-26T23:11:48Z  CHANGE    Slice 3: the download-and-play cluster left SunoBridge for `src/qml_bridge/SunoDownloadSection.hpp/.cpp`, a QObject child of the bridge. It owns the borrow of the one `SunoDownloader`, the per-clip status, the save-vs-play latch (`playRequestClipId_`), the batch refusal accounting and the `downloadStateChanged` wording. `vc::suno::SunoDownloader` still owns every request and every byte written to disk.
2026-10-26T23:11:48Z  CHANGE    The clip title is asked of the bridge through a provider callback, so the section keeps no second copy of the library cache. The section asks for a status or error message instead of writing into another object's state; the bridge keeps its two channels. `clipSaved`, `clipSaveRefused` and `clipDownloadSettled` keep their names, arguments and order.
2026-10-26T23:11:48Z  CHANGE    Lifetime preserved and tightened: the borrow is dropped on sign-out and on a controller swap BEFORE the outgoing controller dies (the old code disconnected the downloader explicitly for the same reason), and the latches are cleared with it, so the next controller's first event cannot be judged by the old request's answer. The moved code is otherwise a pure move: the service check still precedes the empty-batch check, and the refusal sentences are unchanged.
2026-10-26T23:11:48Z  CHANGE    New test suite `tests/unit/qml_bridge/test_SunoDownloadSection.cpp` pins the fail-closed boundary: status empty before any transfer; a save with no controller says no download service is attached and raises no per-clip refusal; the empty batch reports the missing service because the service check comes first; a play with no controller says the clip has no playable media; an empty id is refused before anything else; detach is safe and announces nothing; the title provider is optional.
2026-10-26T23:11:48Z  CHANGE    A morph edit corrupted seven member initializers in `SunoBridge.hpp` (`{false);` instead of `{false};`), which moc reported as the misleading "Namespace declaration lacks Q_NAMESPACE macro". The file was repaired and the build is clean; the lesson for the next agent is that an edit tool that rewrites a block can corrupt a neighbouring line, so a build failure pointing at a namespace is worth bisecting against the committed header.
2026-10-26T23:11:48Z  CHANGE    Sizes after both slices: `SunoBridge.cpp` 1645 -> 1328 LOC, `SunoBridge.hpp` 429 -> 395 LOC, with `SunoMutationsSection` 291+99 and `SunoDownloadSection` 262+94. The bridge's remaining clusters are QML-adapter work (translation, caching, naming) and were deliberately left in the adapter.
